  "scope": "Dijkstra's unchanged TICK (applyTickNoEvents) of the Leios testnet build, with the globals mkShelleyGlobals makes of each network's Shelley genesis file and a fixed epoch size, applied to the NewEpochState of two Leios-build state files (a devnet's first Dijkstra state, and the public Leios testnet at epoch 100) along two paths: the first slots of the next two epochs, and the same with a tick at each epoch's reward start point before its boundary; and, up to the first boundary, four states derived from each with the ledger's own lenses and functions (a pool retiring; a pool re-registering with another VRF key hash while a second pool shares its active one, the counts recomputed by populateVRFKeyHashes; both, retiring a third pool or the sharing one) to exercise Dijkstra's POOLREAP. No ledger rule makes the derived states. Each state reached is written with toCBOR at version 12, as a ledger snapshot holds it. The ledger's NewEpochState only: not the consensus layer's ledger state around it (tip, transition, cumulative transaction bytes), nor the header state",
